==Strategy==
Ahirujo only appears once the base is hit, so it is best to wait as long as possible before approaching the base. Doing so will greatly reduce the difficulty of this stage as almost all of the Wild Doges will have already spawned by the time you face Ahirujo. However this is easier said than done, for it would require you to efficiently kill the Wild Doges while keeping the Dark Otters alive long enough for all 18 Wild Doges to spawn. The Wild Doges, coupled with the limited cash at the beginning of the stage, makes it difficult to stall. If you manage to pull this off, however, Ahirujo should appear with very limited support. If you find this stage too difficult, it may be best to instead try [[Woodlands Area 4]].

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Fish Cat]]: Extremely potent counter to Ahirujo. At level 20, he is able to tank three hits from Ahirujo without getting knocked back (assuming Ahirujo does not land a [[Savage Blow]]).
*[[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fried Shrimp Cat]]: Durable anti-Red tanker capable of stalling Ahirujo for long periods of time, and for even longer in his True Form. Struggles against Wild Doges, however.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Dancing Flasher Cat]]: Strong attacker capable of killing the Wild Doges in 3 hits at level 30; 2 in his True Form or with an Attack Up combo.
*[[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] and [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Dragon Cat]]: Attackers with enough range to avoid Ahirujo's LD entirely.
*[[Bath Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Sexy Bathtub Cat]]: Essentially another Dragon Cat with half the cost and Massive Damage against Red. Be wary when using it, as it has longer recharge and cannot survive a Wild Doge hit unless in True Form.

